# 7b-3 (ticket OPUS-7B3-20260929-02): a body root under a deeper path.  pt is a Point declared in the while body; after
# `end: while` the path while\pt\x reads its place (the last iteration's pt: x 2) -- as an assignment's value, and as a
# call's argument, where P0 gives the path as the atoms `while`, `\`, `pt`, `\`, `x` (l2_path_chain: a control body's
# head starts a path as `node` does, not an identifier).  a * 10 + b = 22.  Native only: a Structure field declared in a
# nested body keeps a method out of the walk.  Success 7, anything else 64.
Point:
    int: x 0
    int: y 0
end: Point
fn: nop () int
    return: 0
end: nop
fn: id (int: v) int
    return: v
end: id
fn: test () int
    int: i 0
    while: i < 3
        Point: pt
        pt\x: i
        i: i + 1
    end: while
    nop()
    int: a 0
    a: while\pt\x
    int: b 0
    b: id(while\pt\x)
    int: ok 64
    if: a * 10 + b = 22
        ok: 7
    return: ok
end: test
int: r 0
r: test()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
